exports[`issue body (snapshot) 2`] = `
"Translation notes from \`María López\` for **es** (Español), 3 notes on 2 pages.
Submitted with translate.beekeeperstudio.io, from the pages on \`https://www.beekeeperstudio.io\`.

### 1. \`/pricing/\` · \`p, under "Pricing"\`
English: \`Pay once, use the paid features forever.\`  
Now: \`Paga una vez, usa las funciones de pago para siempre.\`  
New: \`Paga una sola vez y usa las funciones de pago para siempre.\`  
Comment: \`"una sola vez" reads more naturally.\`

### 2. \`footer\` (every page) · \`/\`
English: \`Blog\`  
Now: \`Blog\`  
New: \`Blog técnico\`  
This text is in the site footer: the change applies on every page.

### 3. \`/pricing/\` · \`p, under "Pricing"\`
English: \`Read <a href="/docs">the docs</a>\`  
Now: \`Lee <a href="/docs">la documentación</a>\`  
New: \`Consulta <a href="/docs">los documentos</a>\`  
Lint warnings: \`glossary: "Docs" is usually "Documentación"\`

<details><summary>Machine-readable notes</summary>

\`\`\`yaml
lang: es
site: "https://www.beekeeperstudio.io"
submitted: 2026-10-21T10:14:00Z
notes:
  - path: /pricing/
    key: "Pay once, use the paid features forever."
    scope: null
    where: "p, under \\"Pricing\\""
    current: "Paga una vez, usa las funciones de pago para siempre."
    new: "Paga una sola vez y usa las funciones de pago para siempre."
    comment: "\\"una sola vez\\" reads more naturally."
    apply:
      action: set-explicit
      file: bin/translations/explicit/es.yml
      entry: { path: /pricing/, en: "Pay once, use the paid features forever.", es: "Paga una sola vez y usa las funciones de pago para siempre." }
  - path: /
    key: "Blog"
    scope: footer
    where: "a, under \\"Links\\""
    current: "Blog"
    new: "Blog técnico"
    apply:
      action: set-common
      file: bin/translations/common/es.json
      set: [footer, "Blog", "Blog técnico"]
  - path: /pricing/
    key: "Read <a href=\\"/docs\\">the docs</a>"
    scope: null
    where: "p, under \\"Pricing\\""
    current: "Lee <a href=\\"/docs\\">la documentación</a>"
    new: "Consulta <a href=\\"/docs\\">los documentos</a>"
    warnings:
      - "glossary: \\"Docs\\" is usually \\"Documentación\\""
    apply:
      action: set-explicit
      file: bin/translations/explicit/es.yml
      entry: { path: /pricing/, en: "Read <a href=\\"/docs\\">the docs</a>", es: "Consulta <a href=\\"/docs\\">los documentos</a>" }
\`\`\`

</details>

---
**Applying these notes** (for the agent or person picking this up)

1. Read the YAML block above. For each note, apply its \`apply\` to the named file in this repository:
   - \`set-common\`: set \`common[<scope>][<key>]\` in the JSON file. It changes that string on every page with the include. Keep the file sorted by scope.
   - \`set-explicit\`: in the YAML file, set the language's value of the entry whose \`path\` and \`en\` match, or append the entry if there is none, as \`node bin/translations.mjs pin\` does.

   The notes were written against the live site, which doesn't say where a translation comes from: if something more specific overrides the change (an explicit entry for the page, say, over a common one), change that instead.

   Keep \`explicit/<lang>.yml\` in its existing format (\`yaml.dump\` with \`forceQuotes\`, as \`pin\` does).
2. A note whose English (\`key\`) is no longer on the page is out of date: skip it, and say so on this issue.
3. Run \`node bin/translations.mjs lint\`: it must pass.
4. Commit and open a pull request that closes this issue. The next deploy renders the affected pages again."
`;
